meta {
  name: POST Cancel
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{baseURL}}/centers/{{center_id}}/appointments/{{appointment_id}}/cancel/
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  content-type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "reason": "Customer requested cancellation"
  }
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 30000
}

docs {
  Allowed from confirmed or checked_in. Not from in_progress. Reason required.
  Auth: staff or customer JWT. Customer may only cancel their own profile's appointments (else 404).
  When linked to a therapy program_service: RedemptionHistory scheduled→cancelled.
  sessions_used unchanged. active_appointment on therapy services list becomes null.
  Google Calendar: if the appointment was mirrored, a Google Calendar outbox row is queued after
  commit to delete the event from the fixed shared account's calendar (GOOGLE_CALENDAR_ID).
  google_event_id/google_meet_link are left as-is. Best-effort — if that Google call fails, the
  failure is logged and the cancellation stays saved (the Google event may still exist and need
  manual cleanup). Cancel HTTP success does not mean the Calendar event is already gone.
}
